# BLOQUE 75: the animated sets are specified in TEXT (TOML), and their
# line endings must not depend on WHERE the repository was checked out.
#
# With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) the same blob became
# CRLF or LF depending on the checkout, and the anchors' freshness hash was
# computed over the RAW bytes -- so the freshness check went red on half
# the checkouts, with no change to the art. The hash is now computed over
# normalised text (BLOQUE 74), and this file stops the divergence at the
# source: a TOML file is checked out with LF everywhere.
#
# The scope is deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto` would
# renormalise every tracked file and touch the worktrees of the agents
# working on this repo in parallel.
*.toml text eol=lf
